<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philomelus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 354 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Philomelus was a Phocian general who began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-sacred-war">Third Sacred War</a>. In 356 BCE, after the Amphictyonic Council fined the Phocians, he seized Delphi and used its treasures to hire <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a>. He defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/locrians">Locrians</a> and Boeotians in several battles but was defeated at Neon in 354 BCE and threw himself from a cliff; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/onomarchus">Onomarchus</a> succeeded him.</p></div>
